<article class="env-lemma" id="02K6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02K6">Lemma <span data-tag="02K6">29.37.20</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[rr]_ f \ar[rd]_ p &  &  Y \ar[dl]^ q \\  &  S }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram of morphisms of schemes. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is surjective, and étale, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$p$ is étale, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$q$ is locally of finite presentation<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000648415" id="a0000648415-mark"><sup>1</sup></a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $q$ is étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/02K5" data-tag="02K5">29.35.19</a> we see that $q$ is smooth. Thus we only need to see that $q$ has relative dimension $0$. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/02JS" data-tag="02JS">29.29.2</a> and the fact that $f$ and $p$ have relative dimension $0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>